abstract: >-
  De-identified data and analysis code for a cross-sectional meta-research study of
  the methodological quality of health research from Saudi Arabia. A random sample of
  385 primary human health studies published in 2022 with at least one Saudi-affiliated
  author was drawn from the 5,558 records that a PubMed search for such studies
  returned. Each study was classified by its epidemiological task (descriptive,
  predictive or causal) and appraised with a task-aligned instrument (ITQAN) covering
  random error, selection bias, measurement bias, confounding and missing data. Two of
  thirteen calibrated epidemiologists appraised each study independently, and two
  members of the study team adjudicated their disagreements.
